    "implication": "Single-threaded batch throughput above ~10^5 flows/s covers a 1 Gbps link under a conservative 1 KB mean flow size; a single commodity core is therefore sufficient at campus/edge scale. The binding cost in practice is FEATURE EXTRACTION from the packet stream, not model inference \u2014 a point most ML-IDS papers omit."
